dotProject Mantis module 1.0 - MantisBT integration through the REST API
=======================================================================

What it does
------------
- Links a dotProject project to a MantisBT project (project tab "Mantis").
- Lists the issues of the linked Mantis project.
- Imports selected issues as dotProject tasks (each issue once per project;
  the task links back to the issue).
- Changes the status of selected issues, optionally with a note.
- Creates the Mantis project for a dotProject project (needs a Mantis token
  with the right to create projects).

Requirements
------------
- MantisBT 2.x with the REST API enabled (the default); tested with 2.28.
- PHP curl extension on the dotProject server.

Setup
-----
1. Install the module in System Admin > View Modules.
2. In System Admin > System Configuration > Mantis Integration, set the Mantis
   address, for example https://bugs.example.org. It must be HTTPS; "Allow
   HTTP for Mantis" exists only for a local test installation.
3. Each user creates an API token in Mantis (My Account > API Tokens) and
   enters it on the module page (Mantis > Mantis API token). Mantis then
   applies that user's own Mantis permissions; dotProject never sends Mantis
   anything about the dotProject account.
4. In a project's Mantis tab, link the project to a Mantis project (or create
   it in Mantis).

Permissions
-----------
- Viewing the tab: access to the Mantis module and a stored token.
- Linking, unlinking, creating, importing: edit rights on the project and on
  the Mantis module (importing also needs the right to add tasks).
- Changing status: edit rights on the Mantis module; Mantis decides whether
  the token's user may change the issue.

Upgrading from 0.2
------------------
0.2 talked XML-RPC to a server side copied into Mantis, sent each user's
dotProject password hash to Mantis and matched projects by name. That server
side, the XML-RPC client and the dotProject core patch are gone, and the
"Mantis Integration" project field is removed on upgrade: link each project
again from its Mantis tab, and have each user enter an API token.

Stored data
-----------
Tables mantis_user_tokens (one token per user, never shown again after it is
saved), mantis_projects (dotProject project -> Mantis project) and
mantis_task_issues (tasks created from issues). The tokens are stored as
entered, like other credentials in the dotProject database: restrict access
to the database accordingly. Removing the module drops the three tables.

